.  \n\nPeng B3 gives me a pung for possible All Pungs (6 points) plus maybe Pung of Simples (2 points) if B3 counts (it\u2019s simple), or mixed patterns.  \n\nBut given opponents\u2019 melds: across player has B456 chow and F1 pung \u2014 F1 is dead, B5 dead. Next player has no melds. Previous player none. So maybe they are collecting certain suits.  \n\nDiscarding after Peng would be from W6, W8, T3, J1 \u2014 likely discard J1 (only one, no pair) or W6/W8. That might give away info.  \n\nThe safest is to pass, keep hand flexible, try to draw into a pair for J1 or sequence for W6/W8/T3.  \n\n**Final choice: Pass.**  \n\n**Answer:** Pass"}
